    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A buildId is a locally unique identifier used by a builder to identify a unique
instance of a build produced by it.</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A buildId is a locally unique identifier used by a builder to identify a unique
instance of a build produced by it.</skos:definition>
    <skos:note xml:lang="en">A buildId is a locally unique identifier to identify a unique instance of a
build, according to the buildType.

This identifier differs based on build toolchain, platform, or naming
convention used by an organization or standard.</skos:note>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
