  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/lineRange">
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">lineRange</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines the line range in the original host file that the snippet information
applies to.</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Defines the line range in the original host file that the snippet information
applies to.</skos:definition>
    <skos:note xml:lang="en">This field defines the line range in the original host file that the snippet
information applies to.

If there is a disagreement between the byte range and line range, the byte
range values will take precedence.

A range of lines is a convenient reference for those files where there is a
known line delimiter.
The choice was made to start the numbering of the lines at 1 to be consistent
with the W3C pointer method vocabulary.</skos:note>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/PositiveIntegerRange"/>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
